# Captive Studio Editor Contract

Follow this rule whenever building or editing Captive Studio-compatible client sites.

The source specification is `client-site-spec.md`. If there is a conflict, the source specification wins.

## Production Content

Production pages read from local JSON files in `/content/`.

Content files use this shape:

```json
{
  "templateKey": "homepage",
  "slug": "home",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Page title",
    "description": "Page description"
  },
  "content": {},
  "publishedAt": "2026-04-28T00:00:00.000Z"
}
```

## Preview Content

The preview route `/preview/[pageId]?editor=1` fetches draft content from Captive Studio and renders the matching template in editor mode.

Preview mode must include:

- `EditorModeProvider`.
- `EditorInstrumentation`.
- `postMessage` support for ready, hover, select, refresh, highlight, and clearHighlight.

## Editable Fields

Every editable text field must use `EditableText`.

Every editable image field must use `EditableImage`.

Every field path must exactly match the JSON structure:

```txt
hero.headline
hero.image
features[0].title
features[2].body
cta.buttonLabel
```

Editable elements must emit:

```txt
data-field-path
data-field-type
```

only in editor mode.

## Images

Never store editable images as bare strings.

Use:

```json
{
  "url": "https://cdn.example.com/image.jpg",
  "width": 1920,
  "height": 1080,
  "alt": "Descriptive alt text"
}
```

## Do Not

- Do not hardcode client-editable text in JSX.
- Do not hardcode editable image URLs in JSX.
- Do not invent field path formats.
- Do not read from Supabase on production routes.
- Do not add client authentication to production routes.
- Do not allow clients to add, remove, or reorder fixed template sections unless the product spec changes.

